# README Authoring Rules

## Role

- MUST treat the README as the project's entry manual with purpose, structure, and steps to start using it.
- MUST move detailed specifications, exceptions, and internal logic to code or dedicated documentation.
- MUST keep the README short enough to read on one screen.

## Required Sections

- MUST write purpose as a bullet list immediately under `# Title` (2 to 4 items).
- MUST NOT add `## 概要`.
- MUST NOT add `クイックスタート`.
- MUST NOT insert `---` between sections.

### Pattern A (split procedures)

- MUST use these `##` sections in this order: `構成`, `セットアップ`, `使い方`, `その他`.

### Pattern B (single linear flow)

- MUST use these `##` sections in this order: `構成`, `基本フロー`, `その他`.
- MUST choose Pattern B when the workflow is linear from first use through completion.
- MUST keep `## 基本フロー` as a numbered list only, with at most 6 steps.
- MUST NOT mix Pattern A and Pattern B procedure headings in the same README.

## Writing Rules

### Overall Flow

| Order | Content | Location |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Purpose and outcome | Bullet list under `# Title` (2 to 4 items) |
| 2 | Structure (paths and roles) | Under `## 構成` |
| 3 | Procedures | Pattern A: `セットアップ` and `使い方` / Pattern B: `基本フロー` |

- MUST write one sentence per purpose bullet under the title.
- MUST NOT lead with procedures before purpose is clear under the title.
- MUST use bullets or tables for structure and numbered lists for procedures.
- MUST NOT mix structure and procedures in the same paragraph.
- MUST NOT add background or specification text inside procedural sections.
- MUST NOT start procedures with clone-only or environment-only steps; start from the core workflow.

### Per Section

| Section | Content | Limits |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Under `# Title` | What the project is and what it enables | 2 to 4 bullets; one sentence per bullet |
| `構成` | Main folders and files with roles | One item per line |
| `セットアップ` | First-use steps (Pattern A) | Numbered list only; at most 5 steps |
| `使い方` | Update, distribution, routine operation (Pattern A) | MUST NOT duplicate first-use steps |
| `基本フロー` | End-to-end steps (Pattern B) | Numbered list only; at most 6 steps |
| `その他` | Minimal terms and pointers to detailed docs | Keep minimal; delete when it grows |

### Do Not Write in README

- Clone, Cursor launch, or similar prerequisite bullets before the procedure list.
- A first step that is only clone or environment setup without core workflow content.
- Detailed operational constraints that belong in dedicated README files or runbooks.
- Headings such as `### このプロジェクトについて` when `## 構成` is clearer.
- Horizontal rules (`---`) between sections.

## Prohibited Content

- NEVER write specifications, exception handling, or internal logic in the README.
- NEVER add `## 概要` or `### このプロジェクトについて`.
- NEVER repeat the same caution across sections.
- NEVER lead with procedures before purpose appears under the title.
- NEVER let the README exceed one-screen length.
- NEVER mix Pattern A and Pattern B procedure sections.
- NEVER insert `---` between sections.

## Final Check

- MUST verify purpose is clear from the title and the bullets immediately below it.
- MUST verify structure is listed under `## 構成`.
- MUST verify linear workflows use `基本フロー` only, and split workflows use `セットアップ` and `使い方`.
- MUST verify the first procedure step is not clone-only or environment-only.
- MUST verify structure and procedures are separated.
- MUST verify steps are executable by copy-paste.
- MUST verify no `---` appears between sections.
- MUST rewrite the README when any check fails.
